From: dtrace.nix maintainers
Subject: tests: synchronize process and USDT fixtures explicitly

Software-emulated guests can spend several seconds compiling and attaching a
DTrace program.  Do not use fixed sleeps, or the creation of DTrace's output
file, as evidence that the consumer and its probes are ready.  Keep targets
alive until enablement, use BEGIN handshakes for consumers, and derive bounded
polling deadlines from the runner's timeout.

Also make the pid dash fixture non-PIE because that test intentionally compares
link-time absolute addresses, and compare switchrate delays relative to the
same guest's startup overhead.

